  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Monochromatic light of wavelength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span> in air is incident normally on a thin soap film of thickness <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> and refractive index <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n\"></span>. The film is surrounded by air on both sides. Which of the following represents a thickness <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> that results in the maximum intensity of the reflected light?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = \\frac{\\lambda}{2n}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = \\frac{\\lambda}{4n}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = \\frac{\\lambda}{n}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = \\frac{3\\lambda}{2n}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
